  "worked_solution": "Notice that the sets are overlapping since\n\n$$\n{-2,-1,0}\\cap {0,1,2}={0}\\ne \u2205.\n$$\n\nSo, for each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is tagged with the corresponding index, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{\u2217}={(-2,1),(-1,1),(0,1)} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{\u2217}={(0,2),(1,2),(2,2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}\u2294{A}_{2} & ={-2,-1,0}\u2294{0,1,2} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{\u2217}\\cup {A}_{2}^{\u2217} \\\\  & ={(-2,1),(-1,1),(0,1)}\\cup {(0,2),(1,2),(2,2)} \\\\  & ={(-2,1),(-1,1),(0,1),(0,2),(1,2),(2,2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
